A||N||20||Northstar308||Fiero Targa Roof||||5||
Z||000000||Northstar308||10-18-2000||02:34 PM||||Anybody have any information on how much work/expense it is to add a targa roof to a fiero. I was looking at John Norman's Fiero that's currently on eBay and I would love to do this to my car.   Looks like he added a rollcage internally, but not sure of much else.  Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||10-18-2000||02:50 PM||||There used to be a Targa kit produced, but it has been discontinued. <BR>You just about have to build in some sort of bracing when you remove the roof, as it is a structural member of the space-frame. If you don't, the car will flex. A bunch. <BR>At least one of the folks here has a Targa. (80's guy, I think.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-18-2000||05:19 PM||||Wow, I was just thinking about the same thing the other day.<BR>Please let me know what you find out.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Northstar308||10-18-2000||05:46 PM||||Anybody else know of this 'targa kit' that may have been offered?  Who manufactured it?  How much was it?  What it included?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-18-2000||05:56 PM||||I just got off the phone with John.  Pro street style roll cage, custom X crossmember, and lots of extra bracing underneath.  He said that he has an external fuel pump.  Good thing since you'd have to cut the X to get the tank out.  Man, I drool everytime I see his car.  Too bad I don't have an extra 18 grand. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||10-18-2000||06:50 PM||||Below is a scan of a flyer that I got from Pisa in October '96. The targa is manufactured by Corson Motorsports, they also offered V8 conversion kits. I don't know if it's still available or not, but a call or email to Pisa would answer that. There should be some old posts here about the frame stiffening, do a search for convertibles and such. The steel unedrcarriage can be contrutcted to allow removal of the fuel tank.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targa.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Northstar308||10-18-2000||10:17 PM||||Josh is drooling now...I'll call PISA tomorrow.  Didn't they end up buying Corson?  This is EXACTLY what I have been looking for!  No one has an extra kit laying around do they?<BR>Josh||||reg||14
Z||000007||Raydar||10-19-2000||12:39 AM||||Ed Parks used to have one in his showroom. It wasn't for sale, though.<BR>I called PISA, back in the spring. The gentleman who answered said that the Targa roof had gone out of production several years ago, and was no longer available. I hope that I was under the influence of something, and just dreamed it, though. Sure would like one.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||10-19-2000||09:30 AM||||One of my Fiero Club (Suncoast Fieros)members just bought a Targa Fiero. I'll try to hook up with him at the next meeting (11/8) and arrange to get some detailed photos. I don't know if it's a kit targa or home-made but, I'll let you know.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000009||Oreif||10-19-2000||11:12 AM||||There is a member "Coyote" who is converting an 84 into a convertable. He did the same thing that Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes Fiero does. He drives square stock into the frame rails and attaches them to strut/shock towers. So there is nothing blocking the gas tank and you cannot see the braces. I know that Bob has done Targa tops before and a few convertables. Give him a call and see what he would charge. <BR>Bob's number is 217-379-9140.<BR>If you are handy with a welder (or know someone who is) I'm sure Bob cane fill you in on exactly how to do it. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Northstar308||10-19-2000||12:07 PM||||Called Bob, <BR>He says he hasn't done one (though he figured he could do one if I had a targa panel) yet, mainly does ttops.  I'm waiting on a call back from PISA; I'll keep updating here what I find.<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000011||CozmoPooky||10-19-2000||02:14 PM||||Hi,<BR>This is my first post on an awesome Fiero resource! I just bought the Targa mrfixit58 referred to earlier. Here is a link to photopoint for pics:<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1247137&a=9215244" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1247137&a=9215244</A> <BR>I have no idea who made the kit (looks professionally done, tho) but it does have a bolted in X-frame underneath. Can't wait to get it on the road!<P>------------------<BR>Bob Cardone (CozmoPooky)<BR>'87 Coupe<BR>'85 2M6 Targa||||reg||1
Z||000012||William||10-19-2000||09:24 PM||||Fabulous! I too have a 85 2m6 and after seeing all the mods and upgrades around, I have always thought that the 85 2m6 with targa top and full leather interior would be the ultimate fiero. You have now confirmed my beliefs. Wanna trade?<p>[This message has been edited by William (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfixit58||10-19-2000||10:13 PM||||Hey Bob,<P>Welcome to the forum. Have you just been lurking and waiting for someone to talk about your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ? I'm glad to see the photos of your car and can't wait to see it in person. Are you bringing it to the next club meeting?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000014||CozmoPooky||10-20-2000||07:58 AM||||You're right Roy...  I *discovered* this forum about two weeks ago and have been [lurking]   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> deep in the archives ever since.  What an awesome resource of info on our unique cars!  I hope to have the Targa at the next Suncoast Fieros meeting, but I have to fix a stripped out leaky water pump bolt first.  Besides the leak, the car runs great even tho it looks like badgers lived in it. If anyone wants more detailed pics, measurements or has questions on the Targa top let me know.  I did find (on the Mich. club site) a person selling Targa kits- The post is from July, I know nothing of the kits and have not talked to the person but I'll post this info for whoever is interested.<BR>Targa Top Kits<BR>I have 5 targa top kits complete with all parts to install on any 2m4 Fiero.<BR>$1500 each.<BR>Rochester Hills, Mich<BR>Website:<BR>Email: dgziehm@tir.com &lt;mailto:dgziehm@tir.com&gt; | Phone:<BR>Ad #: 100 |||209.216.94.1||reg||10
Z||000015||mbramble||10-20-2000||09:23 AM||||OK, let me jump off topic here and ask about the white '87 SC in one of the photos with the Targa...<P>What is an SC (Sports Coupe??).??  Looks like a Coupe with an aero fascia but a normal coupe rear fascia and no ground effects.  That's what my car looks like now after replacing the coupe nose with an aero.  May add f/x and a GT rear fascia in the future but do I now basically have a SC??<P>Or has a different fascia been put on the white 87 SC in the Targa photos???<P>Thanks.....<P><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||baldlobo||10-20-2000||12:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mbramble:<BR><B>OK, let me jump off topic here and ask about the '87 SC in one of the photos with Targa...<P>What is an SC (Sports Coupe??).??  Looks like a Coupe with an aero fascia but a normal coupe rear fascia and no ground effects.  That's what my car looks like now after replacing the coupe nose with an aero.  May had f/x and a GT rear fascia in the future but do I now basically have a SC??<P>Thanks.....<P>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-20-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>an SC is just a coupe with more options and as far as I know they didn't come with the aero fascia or any other body changes.<BR>ps. I have an 84 SC(really good car). <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||mbramble||10-20-2000||01:40 PM||||This is the photo I am talking about.  Is the white car an SC because it has an aero fascia, or was that fascia added on to an SC??? <P>I don't think I'll ever get PIP to work so here is a link....<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1247137&a=9215244&p=29975002" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1247137&a=9215244&p=29975002</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||william_thorniii||10-20-2000||01:47 PM||||mbramble,<P>An SC is just one of the coupe variations.  There is no visual difference between SC (Sport Coupe) and EC (Econo Coupe).  The fascia as you have described it must have been retrofitted to this coupe.  <P>Sounds like you need to find Mark Corbin... and spend the best $4 of your life on the Fiero spotters guide.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000019||CozmoPooky||10-20-2000||03:10 PM||||The VIN on the '87 in the pic says it is a plain vanilla Duke Coupe. Whoever had it before me put on the aero fascia, dual exhausts, GT gauges and lace wheels. I don't think they made a SC in '87, I mislabeled the pic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> in ignorance. I think the combo looks good, a shame it doesn't go as fast as it looks. That will change someday. (V8??)<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob Cardone (CozmoPooky)<BR>'87 Coupe<BR>'85 2M6 Targa||||reg||1
Z||000020||mbramble||10-20-2000||05:57 PM||||Thanks for clearing that up about the SC.  I think it looks good, too.  In fact mine looks just the same!!  Except it is the '87 medium red.  I painted the new aero fasica two nights ago (with cans of Dupli-Color), sanded the clear coat on the front hood and re-clear coated it and clear coated the new paint on the fasica.  Looks pretty darned good.  I painted the new roof that I put on (with a sunroof) last night and will sand/clear coat it whenever my son gets the car home from school.  Will post a couple of photos when it done.<BR>||||reg||1
